# Coming and going in Russian: ухожу, приезжаю, сходи
subtitle: "Every day or just once in Russian: ухожу́ beside ушёл, приезжа́ю beside прие́хал, and сходи́ for a trip there and back."
tags: ["russian","verbs of motion","уходить","приезжать","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/motion-prefixes","grammar/aspect"]
thumb: "band \"Once, or every day?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Don't forget in Russian: aspect after не","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/135-russian-dont-forget.cast"}

## Coming and going in Russian: ухожу, приезжаю, сходи
stress: new
level: basic
shuffle: true
heading: false

